# Copy to .env and adjust. No real secret should ever be committed.

# Port published on the host by the application. Without this variable, it is 3010.
# Change it if 3010 is already taken on your machine — it is the only place that
# needs to change, and the address becomes http://localhost:<value>.
# PORTA_HOST=3010

# Postgres credentials (also used by compose.yaml to bring the database up).
POSTGRES_USER=colecao_pokemon
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=troque-esta-senha
POSTGRES_DB=colecao_pokemon

# Full connection string used by the app and by the scripts (migrate, sync).
# Inside Docker Compose the host is the name of the database service ("db").
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://colecao_pokemon:troque-esta-senha@db:5432/colecao_pokemon

# Politeness of the TCGdex client (optional — the code defaults are the values
# below). Do not raise them without a reason: with 40 requests in parallel and
# no rate ceiling, our IP was blocked in their firewall on 2026-08-25.
# Global ceiling of requests per second against the API.
# SYNC_REQ_POR_SEGUNDO=6
# How many requests stay in flight at the same time.
# SYNC_CONCORRENCIA_CARDS=4
# SYNC_CONCORRENCIA_SETS=2
# User-Agent sent to TCGdex — an anonymous client at volume is the first one to
# get blocked, and identifying the client is a hard rule of this project
# (AGENTS.md). The code default already identifies the project; this variable
# exists for anyone who wants to add a contact, and .env is not versioned.
# SYNC_USER_AGENT=personal-pokemon-tcg-collection/0.1 (personal install; contact: you@example.com)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LigaPokemon price collector
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Interval between two requests to their site, in seconds.
#
# WITHOUT this variable, the default is to OBEY THEIR robots.txt: the
# `Crawl-delay` is read live (today, 360 s) and whatever is written there is
# what applies. If they loosen it, you benefit the same day; if they tighten
# it, you obey the same day. A read failure (network down, 5xx, malformed
# file) falls back to the conservative value, never to the aggressive one.
#
# The cost of the default is time: the 161 empty slots of a Pokédex take ~16
# hours at 360 s, against ~12 minutes at 3 s. The scan runs in the background,
# writes after every slot and, when triggered again, skips the slots queried in
# the last 24 hours — so a container restart does not send it back to the start.
#
# Setting the variable makes the value you give it the one that applies, and
# the choice is yours. An honest note from whoever maintains the project:
# **3 seconds is the value this project used day to day, with no trouble** —
# above what the file asks for, and below what the browser itself would
# generate opening the same pages (each page in the browser pulls dozens of
# images and scripts that the collector does not pull). That is the experience
# of ONE installation, not a promise: lowering the interval is the decision and
# the risk of whoever configures it, and the risk is an IP block — this server
# already took one from TCGdex on 2026-08-25, out of haste.
#
# The routes stay restricted to cards/search and cards/card at any value.
# LIGA_INTERVALO_SEGUNDOS=3

# Path, on the HOST, of the local clone of tcgdex/cards-database (git clone
# --depth 1 https://github.com/tcgdex/cards-database.git <path>) — used only
# by compose.yaml to mount the clone (read-only) inside the container at
# /upstream-dados-tcgdex. A relative path is resolved from the project
# folder; the default below is the same one compose.yaml uses when the
# variable is not set. It does not need to exist if you are not going to run
# `pnpm importar:catalogo-repo`.
# The recommendation is to clone the repository wherever you want and point
# this at it; the default (./.dados/tcgdex-cards-database) is just an empty
# mount point, versioned so that Docker does not create it as root. See README.
# TCGDEX_REPO_HOST_PATH=/path/to/tcgdex-cards-database

# Path INSIDE the container where the local image files live — the ones the
# user supplies for a card with no photo (upload or downloaded from a URL —
# lib/armazenamento-imagens.ts). compose.yaml already mounts a named Docker
# volume (`imagens_locais`) at this path; it only needs to change if you
# change the volume's destination as well. Outside Docker (local `pnpm dev`),
# without this variable the folder falls back to `.dados/imagens-locais` in
# the workspace.
# IMAGENS_LOCAIS_DIR=/dados/imagens-locais
